{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-3389",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-3389: Important priority package update for kernel",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-09 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-11 02:16:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-99082:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: x86: Use active memslots for the per-vCPU MMIO cache\n\nCVE-2026-99053:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntipc: hold a reference to nodes found by link name\n\nCVE-2026-98857:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipvs: bound LBLCR and LBLC cache growth\n\nCVE-2026-98846:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsctp: check RCV_SHUTDOWN after the sendmsg connect wait\n\nCVE-2026-98805:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntipc: prevent GCM nonce reuse on peer key changes\n\nCVE-2026-98715:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: SVM: Preserve TLB control (i.e. pending TLB flush) on failed VMRUN\n\nCVE-2026-98466:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Transfer the hyp stack pages out of the host stage-2\n\nCVE-2026-98454:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix create context out-of-bounds reads\n\nCVE-2026-98033:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Preserve inner map identity in callback frames\n\nCVE-2026-97563:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: reject out-of-bounds DataOffset in CIFSSMBRead()\n\nCVE-2026-90036:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during blocked-lock reaping\n\nCVE-2026-89659:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during delegation revoke\n\nCVE-2026-89633:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix OOB read/write from unvalidated DataOffset in coalesce_t2()\n\nCVE-2026-74752:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use\n\nCVE-2026-74356:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvhost: fix vhost_get_avail_idx for a non empty ring\n",
